               note: "The crackers are the traditional thickener, not a hack, and they matter. Without them the sauce is a soup that slides straight off the potato.",
               shortcut: "Feta blended with a little extra milk stands in for queso fresco. Cut the added salt in half, since feta brings its own."),
        Recipe(dishID: "peru-anticucho", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 30, cookMinutes: 30, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 lb", item: "beef heart, trimmed (or sirloin, the common home substitute)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "ají panca paste (or 2 tbsp ancho chile powder mixed with oil)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/4 cup", item: "red wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "4", item: "garlic cloves, minced"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "ground cumin"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "dried oregano"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/4 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "vegetable oil"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 lb", item: "small potatoes, boiled"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "8", item: "wooden or metal skewers"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for 30 minutes so they survive the fire.",
                   "Trim the beef heart of any silverskin and fat, and cut it into flat pieces roughly 1 1/2 inches square and 1/2 inch thick.",
                   "Whisk the ají panca paste, vinegar, garlic, cumin, oregano, salt and 2 tablespoons of the oil into a loose marinade.",
                   "Toss the meat in the marinade and refrigerate at least 20 minutes, or up to 4 hours for deeper flavor. Reserve a spoonful of marinade for basting.",
                   "Thread the meat flat onto the skewers, three or four pieces each, so every piece can touch the heat.",
                   "Grill over the hottest part of a charcoal or gas grill, or under a scorching broiler, 2 to 3 minutes per side, basting once, until charred outside and just pink within.",
                   "Rest the skewers 2 minutes and serve with the boiled potatoes, which belong under the meat to catch the drippings.",
               ],
               note: "Heart is a muscle that goes from tender to rubber in about a minute, so stand at the grill and pull the skewers while the centers are still rosy.",
               shortcut: "Sirloin cubes take the same marinade and forgive an extra minute of cooking, at the cost of the mineral depth that makes anticuchos themselves."),
        Recipe(dishID: "peru-causa", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 40, cookMinutes: 25, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "yukon gold potatoes"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "ají amarillo paste"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3", item: "limes, juiced"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "vegetable oil"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/4 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 cups", item: "cooked chicken, finely shredded"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "mayonnaise"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "ripe avocados, sliced thin"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/4", item: "red onion, minced"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "hard-boiled eggs, sliced, for the top"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Boil the potatoes whole in salted water until completely tender, about 25 minutes, then drain and peel while still hot.",
                   "Rice or mash the potatoes until absolutely smooth, with no lumps, and let them cool to warm.",
                   "Work the ají amarillo paste, lime juice, oil and salt into the potatoes with your hands until the mash is yellow, tangy and holds together like soft dough. Cool fully.",
                   "Mix the shredded chicken with the mayonnaise and minced onion, and season it with salt and a squeeze of lime.",
                   "Press half the potato dough into an even layer in a loaf pan or springform lined with plastic wrap.",
                   "Cover with the chicken salad, then a layer of avocado slices, then press the remaining potato dough evenly over the top.",
                   "Chill at least 1 hour, then unmold, top with sliced egg, and cut into thick slices with a wet knife.",
               ],
               note: "Season the potato until it tastes slightly too sharp on its own. Cold dulls everything, and a timid causa is just mashed potato in a mold.",
               shortcut: "Skip the mold and layer it in individual glasses like a parfait. It sets faster, unmolds never, and looks intentional."),
        Recipe(dishID: "peru-pachamanca", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 30, cookMinutes: 150, difficulty: 3,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 lb", item: "lamb shoulder, cut in large chunks"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 lb", item: "pork shoulder, cut in large chunks"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "huacatay paste (jarred, from a latin market; or blended mint, cilantro and basil)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "6", item: "garlic cloves"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "ground cumin"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/4 cup", item: "red wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "small potatoes, scrubbed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 lb", item: "frozen fava beans (or lima beans), thawed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "ears of corn, cut in thirds"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 package", item: "banana leaves (or parchment and foil)"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Blend the huacatay paste, garlic, cumin, vinegar, salt and a splash of water into a thick green marinade.",
                   "Toss the lamb and pork in two-thirds of the marinade and refrigerate at least 30 minutes, or overnight.",
                   "Heat the oven to 325°F and line a deep roasting pan or large Dutch oven with banana leaves, letting them hang over the sides.",
                   "Lay the potatoes on the bottom, since they take the longest, then the marinated meats, then the corn and favas, spooning the reserved marinade over the vegetables.",
                   "Fold the leaves over everything, cover tightly with a lid or a double layer of foil, and bake for 2 1/2 hours without peeking.",
                   "Check the meat: it should pull apart at a touch, and the potatoes should be floury right through. Give it 20 more covered minutes if not.",
                   "Open the leaves at the table so everyone gets the burst of green steam, and serve straight from the pot with the juices spooned over.",
               ],
               note: "This is the oven translation of an earth pit, and it says so proudly. The sealed leaves and the long unopened bake are what keep the highland character.",
               shortcut: "Use only pork shoulder instead of two meats. One less package, no flavor argument at the table, and the leftovers are less confusing."),
        Recipe(dishID: "peru-picarones", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 45, cookMinutes: 40, difficulty: 3,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "butternut squash, peeled and cubed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "sweet potato, peeled and cubed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 1/2 cups", item: "all-purpose flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 1/4 tsp", item: "instant yeast"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "sugar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "anise seed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "8 oz", item: "piloncillo or dark brown sugar (the chancaca substitute)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 strips", item: "orange peel"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "cinnamon stick"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "whole cloves"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "6 cups", item: "vegetable oil, for frying"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Boil the squash and sweet potato until completely soft, about 15 minutes, then drain, reserving a cup of the cooking water, and mash until smooth. Cool to warm.",
                   "Mix the mash with the flour, yeast, sugar, salt, anise seed and enough reserved cooking water to make a very soft, sticky, stretchy dough. Beat it by hand for 5 minutes.",
                   "Cover and let the dough rise until doubled and bubbly, about 1 hour.",
                   "Meanwhile, simmer the piloncillo with 1 cup water, the orange peel, cinnamon and cloves until it turns into a syrup that coats a spoon, about 15 minutes. Keep warm.",
                   "Heat the oil in a deep pot to 360°F. Set a bowl of salted water beside it for your hands.",
                   "With wet fingers, scoop a handful of dough, poke a hole through the center, and stretch it into a rough ring as you lower it into the oil.",
                   "Fry two or three rings at a time, turning once, until puffed and deep gold, about 2 minutes per side. Drain on a rack.",
                   "Stack the hot rings in shallow bowls and pour the warm spiced syrup generously over them. Eat immediately, with fingers.",
               ],
               note: "The dough should feel too wet to shape, which is exactly right. Wet hands and a fast drop into the oil are the entire technique.",
               shortcut: "Canned pumpkin replaces the boiled squash and skips a pot. The rings taste slightly earthier and nobody in the room will object."),
    ]

